From: Vemloir <Vemloir@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:20:49 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Conversion: affinity-weighted Hessians for block-sparse
 experts (--moe_affinity_eps)

Each expert is quantized against its own Hessian with calibration tokens weighted by
eps + the expert's router affinity relative to its mean, instead of one shared unweighted
gate/up Hessian per layer. Down Hessians accumulate the weighted sum during capture; gate/up
Hessians are built from a sampled set of rows a few experts at a time before quantization,
so memory stays bounded (see conversion/moe_affinity.py).

